 				"_round167_note": "ROUND 167 (Chris, ENGS201-01). In reoMode (a bilingual module OR any module the broad mtkFlag flags), a free-body table that ALL the bilingual handlers decline falls through to a cv2-interactive 'bilingual-unbuilt' placeholder that keeps the raw WT [tag] text BY DESIGN. That is right for an un-built widget/spec table, but a CLEAN STRUCTURAL LAYOUT table (a side-by-side image|body panel, every cell led by a structural [tag]) is NOT a widget — the human renders it as a row>col GRID, and the reoMode path was BYPASSING the layout-table grid that the normal (non-reo) path already runs. So ENGS201-01's 'Origin stories' image|body table shipped as the placeholder and LEAKED [body]/[image] as visible frontend text inside the box. FIX: before the placeholder, try TablesAndGrids.layoutTableGrid (the SAME detector the normal path uses — single-row or all-cells-tagged only, and it BAILS on any widget-member cell tag). A grid is emitted for a clean layout table; a widget/spec/data table still returns null and keeps the placeholder untouched, so no other reoMode table changes and no [tag] is newly exposed. env REOLTABLE_OFF reverts to the always-placeholder behaviour."
